It's indeed as simple as magic whistling your pet into the barracks. I
was trying that from the middle of the corridor between the two barracks.
To get that to work well you need to narrow the room for the pets further
so that they can land close by in an empty square of the barracks instead
of adjacent to you; it might have been done with boulders from a scroll
of earth, but I just used my three pets, for there are only two adjacent
squares available then. The two empty squares within the barracks had
been wobbling around since the soldiers were very excited; with the help
of ESP I waited until the free spaces were close enough to my position.
The essential point is that you need a very tough pet creature that will
be able to overcome these many soldiers with a few hits; I had a dog,
a horse, and a minotaur. Whistling many times, mostly the horse landed
within the barracks (why? just coincidence?), two times the dog, and
finally the minotaur. It only lasted a few moves, then, until the task
was done.

